From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: St0neWan9 <pawamaba@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:09:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: the web page's context menu, drawn by the
 shell

Plan B124. Right-clicking a page showed nothing: Open Arc gives content
no WebContentsViewDelegate (patch 0012), which is where Chrome builds
and shows its menu, and the tab bridge had no HandleContextMenu.

The tab's WebContentsDelegate now handles the menu. It builds Chromium's
model for the click with a RenderViewContextMenuMac subclass that is
never shown (PageMenuModel, oac_context_menu.mm): Chromium's page, link,
image, selection and editable-field items, spelling, the macOS text
services and the profile's chrome.contextMenus items. A snapshot of the
items (each with a role the shell can place) and of what was clicked
goes to -[OACTabDelegate tab:showContextMenu:] as an OACContextMenu.
The shell draws its own NSMenu (Arc's items and order) and shows it with
-popUpMenu:, which keeps Chromium's tasks running while it tracks (Copy
Link to Highlight waits for the page); -performItemWithIdentifier: runs
a Chromium item through the model, so observers and extensions
(contextMenus.onClicked) see it as from Chrome's menu. Items Chromium
updates while open reach itemUpdateHandler. The model is dropped if its
WebContents goes away first.

Commands Chrome runs through a Browser window run here without one:
Reload, Print (the system panel, as File > Print) and Inspect (the
DevTools window on Elements with the element selected, new
openarc::InspectElementAt).

Also:
- -[OACTab requestContextMenuAtPoint:]: the keyboard context menu (the
  page's focused element), for tests and a menu command.
- -[OACProfile actionMenuItemsForExtension:tab:] and
  -performActionMenuItemWithIdentifier:extension:tab:: an extension's
  contexts:["action"] items, for the shell's action menu (B116).
- OACTabDelegate.h: the old willShowContextMenu: method, whose comment
  said the bridge drew Chromium's menu, is replaced.
