+// The web page's right-click menu (plan B124). See OACContextMenu.h.
+//
+// Chrome builds the menu with RenderViewContextMenuMac and shows it with
+// RenderViewContextMenuMacCocoa from its WebContentsViewDelegate, which needs a
+// Views widget (a Chrome browser window). Open Arc keeps the model and drops
+// the drawing: PageMenuModel is a RenderViewContextMenuMac that is never shown
+// by Chromium (Show() does nothing). Its Init() builds Chromium's items for the
+// click, the profile's chrome.contextMenus items included, and the bridge
+// copies them into OACContextMenuItem snapshots for the shell, which draws its
+// own NSMenu. The shell's choice comes back through ExecuteCommand, so
+// observers (Copy Link to Highlight, autofill) and extensions
+// (contextMenus.onClicked) see it as from Chrome's own menu.
+//
+// Commands whose Chrome implementation looks for a Chrome browser window
+// (Reload, Print) are run here directly; the shell runs the ones that need
+// its own UI (Save As…, Open Link in Incognito, Search, Import Passwords).
